    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0277" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.21/244.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Colombian Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I beg you to accept my
                    thanks for your very kind letter of the 9th instant congratulating me on the
                    signature of the convention between the United States and Colombia.</p>
                <p>While it would seem that the convention is not all that you would wish, I feel
                    confident that you will share with me in the hope that <pb facs="0278" n="162"
                        xml:id="pg162"/> it will result in the removal of all friction between the
                    two Governments and in the restoration of their ancient cordial friendship.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
